{
  "description": "The spec documents no errors. Every failure is `{ code, message }`, so these match on `code`. Observed on a live deployment, 2026-10-31 and 2026-11-01: 400 AuthConfigMissingEnvironmentVariable for deleting a variable auth.config.ts reads, EnvironmentVariableNameInvalid, InvalidLogStreamId, InvalidId for a malformed usage limit id, DuplicateUsageLimit; 403 LogStreamingNotEnabled and StreamingExportNotEnabled below the Professional plan, AuditLogsTooOld when the plan keeps 0 days of audit logs, BadDeployKey with no token, OperationNotPermitted for a key that lacks an action; 404 UsageLimitNotFound; 401 MalformedAccessToken. The REST protocol forwards only numeric codes, so matchers read `/code` from the body.",
